export const SIM354 = {
  mech: {
    "1:main": `The laws of a pit and a garbage heap in reshus harabbim. And in it are 2 seifim: A pit in reshus harabbim with a rim around it — if it stands within four tefachim of reshut ha-yachid, it is permitted to draw from it to reshut ha-yachid even if the rim is not ten high; and if it is four away from reshut ha-yachid, one may not draw from it unless the rim is ten high:`,
    "2:main": `A garbage heap in reshus harabbim that is ten high and four wide — if it belongs to the public, it is permitted to throw to it from the adjacent reshut ha-yachid: {Rama: And we are not concerned lest it roll from the garbage heap to reshus harabbim and he come to bring, for there is no way to throw to a garbage heap except repulsive things (Maggid chapter 9 in the name of Rashba)} And if it belongs to an individual it is forbidden, because an individual is apt to empty his garbage heap and people will come to pour there as is their custom and they will end up pouring in reshus harabbim:`,
  },
  bh: {
    "1:_": `Stands. Meaning the pit itself; and the empty space between the well and the wall is makom patur, for less than four the public does not tread there at all. Taz:`,
    "2:_": `Far. Meaning the pit itself — for now it is not makom patur but either reshus harabbim or karmelit in the corner adjacent to reshus harabbim; therefore the pit's rim must be ten high; automatically the bucket with which he draws is above ten and there is no reshus harabbim, and he draws from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via makom patur, for all above ten in reshus harabbim is makom patur — unlike if the rim is less than ten the bucket goes via reshus harabbim and he moves from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim; and see Taz:`,
  },
  beer: {
    "1:_": `Mishna Eruvin 99 according to Rav Huna's resolution`,
    "2:_": `Mishna and Gemara there`,
  },
  gra: {
    "1:_": `Seif 1 — and if it is far. See siman 345 seif 8; and from here until four it is reshus harabbim:`,
    "2:_": `Seif 2 — and we are not concerned. Therefore the mishna mentioned garbage heap and not a rock or mound:`,
  },
  biur: {
    "1:_": `Unless the rim is ten high — and if the pit and window stand on one deyota [in one row] forbidden to lower the bucket from window to pit, for it is passing forbidden from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim even above ten [Magen Avraham]; and it requires further study — behold Yerushalmi chapter HaZorek states passing is only via two like in the Mishkan by the Levites who passed beams from one to another; but not one who passed from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim — and this is brought Shabbos daf 3 Tosafos s.v. "in its making" — see there; and perhaps Yerushalmi's intent is only regarding liability but prohibition exists also for one who passed; and similarly Peri Megadim wrote; perforce the mishna stating l'chatchila permission deals specifically with two deyot:`,
    "2:_": `And four wide — in truth even if it were not four wide it is also permitted, for it is makom patur [Peri Megadim]; and it appears to me he mentioned it because the mishna said a garbage heap ten tefachim high — and if not dealing with four wide, even if it were not, if it were ten high it is also permitted as makom patur:`,
  },
  mb: {
    "1:א": `(1) And a rim — meaning earth around the pit, giving around it to encircle like a wall:`,
    "1:ב": `(2) If it stands — meaning the pit itself:`,
    "1:ג": `(3) Within, etc. — since it is an interruption less than four tefachim between the pit and the wall the public does not tread there at all; perforce it is makom patur:`,
    "1:ד": `(4) To draw from it to reshut ha-yachid — meaning from that side adjacent to reshut ha-yachid — whether standing between the wall and pit taking water from the pit and placing in adjacent reshut ha-yachid, or standing in the house lowering the bucket to the pit via the house window and returning it to the house; and the reason in all this is taking out from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via makom patur:`,
    "1:ה": `(5) Even if the rim is not ten high — meaning only combined with the pit; nevertheless it is reshut ha-yachid of pit and rim; and likewise if there were no rim at all and the pit itself was ten tefachim deep:`,
    "1:ו": `(6) And if it is far, etc. — for now that place is not makom patur but reshus harabbim:`,
    "1:ז": `(7) One may not draw from it — even via window where he moves from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim air, and even though bound in his hand forbidden:`,
    "1:ח": `(8) Unless the rim is, etc. — for then automatically the bucket with which he draws goes above ten where there is makom patur; if so he draws from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via makom patur. And specifically when the window is also ten high from the ground so the bucket never saw reshus harabbim air; and one standing in reshus harabbim lowering a bucket on a rope into a pit ten deep and four wide, filling water and taking out to reshus harabbim — liable; and even though on the bucket alone one need not make him liable since he did not take the rope from reshut ha-yachid when lowering to the pit — nevertheless regarding the water one should make him liable, for he uprooted the water from reshut ha-yachid to reshus harabbim; and even if around the pit there were not reshus harabbim but only karmelit, likewise one should be careful, for in any case there is prohibition. And a bucket hanging on a long tree as we make for our wells to draw, hanging in the pit or even above the pit opposite its air — even if water was in the bucket from before Shabbat without uprooting on Shabbat from the pit — nevertheless careful not to take it from there to lower on the ground around the pit, for he at least made resting on Shabbat; and even holding it in air around the pit Peri Megadim is uncertain if permitted:`,
    "2:א": `(9) Garbage heap in reshus harabbim, etc. — and if standing in karmelit see Peri Megadim:`,
    "2:ב": `(10) That is ten high — for if not ten high karmelit is upon it and forbidden to throw to it from reshut ha-yachid:`,
    "2:ג": `(11) Of the public — for the public throw their refuse and manure there:`,
    "2:ד": `(12) Permitted to throw to it — and even if the garbage heap is far from the wall four tefachim and on the interruption between them there is reshus harabbim — nevertheless permitted to throw to the garbage heap from a window in the house, provided the window is ten high from the ground so the throw is from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via makom patur; and what Mechaber wrote "adjacent to it" comes to exclude if the garbage heap is far from reshut ha-yachid not to throw to the garbage heap lest it fall in reshus harabbim:`,
    "2:ה": `(13) Adjacent to it — and no eruv is needed since there are no dwellers:`,
    "2:ו": `(14) Repulsive things — meaning not needed and he will not come to bring afterward even if it falls:`,
    "2:ז": `(15) As is their custom — that they were accustomed there before, unlike public garbage heap where they do not appoint an overseer for the garbage heap and always it should be ten tefachim high, for all day everyone throws refuse and manure there and its height will not lack:`,
  },
  ma: {
    "1:א": `Within four. For it is makom patur since the public does not tread there:`,
    "1:ב": `One may not draw. Even via window where he moves from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via window — reshus harabbim air; and even though bound in his hand forbidden as written siman 352; and Ritva's forced answer is not needed:`,
    "1:ג": `Rim ten high. Then the bucket goes via makom patur; and specifically when the window is also ten high; and if they are on one deyota forbidden as written seif 17 siman 347; and one standing in reshus harabbim filling from a pit ten deep and four wide — liable; and bound in his hand is not considered, for he uprooted the water from reshut ha-yachid to reshus harabbim — unlike here where he did not uproot water from reshus harabbim and when coming in reshus harabbim air it is bound in his hand:`,
    "2:א": `Garbage heap in reshus harabbim. And no eruv is needed since there are no dwellers:`,
    "2:ב": `Repulsive things. Meaning not needed:`,
  },
  mh: {
    "1:_": `(s.k. 1) Within, etc. makom patur, etc. — see Taz s.k. 1 who brought Ritva's words on this:`,
    "2:א": `(s.k. 2) One may not, etc. moves from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via, etc. as must be:`,
    "2:ב": `And Ritva's forced answer is not needed. See siman 352 s.k. 4 where Magen Avraham brought Ritva's difficulty:`,
  },
  er: {
    "1:_": `[1] [Levush] From a window of reshut ha-yachid, etc. In this permitted even if the window is not ten high — unlike in the second clause where it is four tefachim away, only that the rim ten high requires the window also ten high:`,
    "2:_": `[2] Four tefachim, etc. And Rabbeinu Yerucham daf 95 wrote three tefachim — I wonder, for that is the Gemara Eruvin daf 99 and all poskim; and see Lechem Mishneh chapter 15:`,
  },
  kaf: {
    "1:_": `A) [Seif 1] A pit in reshus harabbim and a rim around it. Meaning earth and stones placed around the mouth of the pit like a wall:`,
    "2:_": `B) There. If it stands within four, etc. Meaning the pit itself stands within four of reshut ha-yachid. Taz s.k. 1. If the pit is four by four from reshut ha-yachid and only the rim reduces it — then if the rim height is not three tefachim that place is reshus harabbim. Machatzit HaShekel part 1; and if the rim is three high and four wide it is karmelit and it is taking out from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via karmelit. Machatzit HaShekel part 2; and if forbidden to pass via karmelit see below part 5:`,
  },
  pm: {
    "1:_": `If now he said the explanation is the pit itself — if the pit is four amot from reshut ha-yachid and only the rim reduces it, then if the rim height is not three tefachim that place is reshus harabbim as siman 345 shortened alleys, etc.; and Rashi Eruvin 99b s.v. "if we say"; and Beit Yosef emended and in Nehar Shalom emended with kaf d'meyuchad — Magen Avraham explained — see there; and it is explained here reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim air — within ten forbidden to take out and throw from one to the other — exempt but forbidden; and Magen Avraham 353b — but Levush here wrote permitted to throw from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim air; and here in filling water it is like passing; and above ten permitted — clear from his language that passing itself is a novelty above ten as one sees in reshus harabbim beginning of chapter 1 and chapter HaZorek — see there — thirty-nine melachot of the Sages bound in hand; and Ateret Rokeach and Magen Avraham 3 and with God's help explained there; and still requires further study; and what Levush further wrote via reshus harabbim or karmelit is from Beit Yosef in Ritva's name in the corner adjacent to reshus harabbim; and Gemara implies specifically via reshut ha-yachid air they decreed lest he take out from reshus harabbim to reshut ha-yachid — not via karmelit which would be decree upon decree; and kaltah not k'mi shehunchah dami; perforce according to those who say now there is no reshus harabbim or karmelit interrupts between pit and reshut ha-yachid — requires further study here; and see letter 2 further from this:`,
    "2:א": `And if now what is written — the pit itself I explained letter 1 — if the rim reduces from four amot width to reshut ha-yachid — if the rim is not three high it is reshus harabbim; and if three high and four wide it is karmelit; and Beit Yosef in Ritva's name that even reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via karmelit forbidden; and see letter 1 here and Magen Avraham; and see Levush:`,
    "2:ב": `Beit Yosef on R' Yochanan Eruvin and Rashi — pit and rim combine; and I did not understand — apparently the words are as their plain meaning; if not combined the pit would be karmelit; and what is written that above ten is makom patur and as the Peri Megadim wrote — since the rim from the pit's edge is ten high — requires much study, for nevertheless from the rim to reshus harabbim there is no ten and it is reshus harabbim air when the bucket goes there; and R' Yochanan said even in proximity he speaks; and as written in Mishna commentaries and in the conditions, etc.; and Ateret Rokeach noticed this — see there; and Shulchan Aruch ruled for halacha in the extreme case — four requires the rim ten high in reshus harabbim; and see nearby with God's help from this:`,
    "2:ג": `And behold Ritva challenged, etc. — from siman 352 seif 2 when it did not rest in reshus harabbim itself but in reshus harabbim air within ten — roll it to him even without much disgrace; and in seif 1 when it rested in reshus harabbim they decreed and permitted only in a trodden place; if so here why forbidden since it did not rest in reshus harabbim air; and Ritva holds as Magen Avraham 352 letter 4 regarding other matters and sacred writings — see there; and Bach answered there b'dieved and here l'chatchila forbidden — this is Ritva's difficulty's answer; but Tur holds here too permitted l'chatchila when it did not rest in reshus harabbim at the edge but hangs in reshus harabbim air — permitted like seif 2 there; and nevertheless require rim height ten, for immediately when uprooting from reshut ha-yachid it comes to makom patur air and from there when descending to reshus harabbim air and from there to reshut ha-yachid window within ten — permitted l'chatchila for Tur even regarding other matters; and Bach's words stand; and Magen Avraham 352 letter 4; and what I wrote one may say:`,
    "2:ד": `And Taz holds there in 352 seif 2 regarding sacred writings specifically permitted; and therefore he challenged thus; and see Magen Avraham there without resting only hanging in karmelit air permitted regarding other matters — unlike Taz here in Rashba's name; and see letter 1 here from this:`,
  },
  taz: {
    "1:_": `If it stands within four tefachim. Meaning the pit itself; and the empty space between pit and wall is makom patur; and even though we rule a tel in reshus harabbim without four is not makom patur unless three high — here is different, for the entire interruption less than four between pit and wall the public does not tread at all; perforce makom patur without four even if not three high; Beit Yosef in Ritva's name; and there is a scribal error there and must read as written:`,
    "2:_": `And if it is far, etc. Meaning the pit itself — for now it is not makom patur but reshus harabbim or karmelit in the corner adjacent to reshus harabbim; therefore the pit rim must be ten high; automatically the drawing bucket is above ten and there is no reshus harabbim and he draws from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via makom patur, for all above ten in reshus harabbim is makom patur — unlike if the rim less than ten the bucket goes via reshus harabbim and moves from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim. Beit Yosef wrote Ritva challenged even when far permitted even without ten high since bound in his hand — meaning the bucket head, for he draws from reshut ha-yachid to reshus harabbim also even shvus there is none as end of chapters siman 352; and Bach answered with forced explanation as Beit Yosef wrote; and Morenu HaRav z"l distinguished that in 352 it is b'dieved and did not rest in reshus harabbim; but here l'chatchila he fills — therefore even though bound in his hand it is like moving from reshut ha-yachid to reshut ha-yachid via reshus harabbim explicitly and forbidden — end; and it appears to me very wondrous there is no difficulty at all, for also in 352 there is concern lest it fall entirely and he come to bring in reshus harabbim; therefore there on a trodden threshold they did not decree thus because of disgrace to sacred writings; and similarly for other things there is reason they did not decree thus; if so here with bound in hand also certainly to decree lest the entire bucket fall from his hand and go downward and he bring from reshus harabbim to his house — and this shvus is certainly forbidden — this appears plain to me and Ritva's intent in his difficulty was hidden from him:`,
  },
  cs: {
    "1:_": `Seif 1 — a pit in reshus harabbim and a rim around it if it stands within four tefachim of reshut ha-yachid, etc. Note: examining the Gemara daf 59 where the Gemara says R' Yochanan said even if you say in proximity — this teaches pit and rim combine to ten; and Rashi explained the mishna is not as we thought the rim alone is ten apart from the pit, rather it means pit and rim together total ten from the pit floor is reshut ha-yachid, etc.; and I wondered on Tur who copied this mishna and wrote even if the rim is not ten high and did not write the extra novelty that even in the pit there is not ten — they combine between them to ten; also siman 347 when Shulchan Aruch copied the law of a ten-deep pit being reshut ha-yachid did not write this extra novelty that pit and rim combine — and it is wondrous and I saw no one who raised this. And while on this I will mention what I was asked: if there is a small pit less than ten and a small mound adjacent less than ten, do they combine to ten to be like a partition regarding not needing eruv — I answered it is not judged as a partition; one: even though the Gemara implies pit and rim combine to ten, Rashi there in Eruvin in his language "and rim around it" implies specifically if encircled on all sides its interior is reshut ha-yachid; but if not encircled on all sides only on one side, even its interior is not judged reshut ha-yachid; and one should not say that regarding its interior it works since it has no partitions on other sides, but regarding being judged in the tel place as a partition it works like a five-high mound and five-high partition that combine — but this is not so, for five-high mound and five-high partition are ten high from the ground; then resting for use is not comfortable so the public do not come and nullify the partition and it is reshut ha-yachid; but here where on other sides it is less than ten, resting for use is comfortable so the public come — therefore not on reshus harabbim. I again saw in Tosafos Shabbos daf 99b and Sefer Tosefta Shabbat siman 345 brought them wrote thus — even though pit and rim combine it is only for its interior to be reshut ha-yachid, not on top — see there; and Sefer Tosefta Shabbat added in their words since it is level on other sides with reshus harabbim ground — and understand my intent in their view; and further it appeared to me support for this law — one may say the reason Tur omitted pit and rim combine to ten is prior to also explain why Tosefta Shabbat wondered why they omitted the explicit law in Tosafos Shabbos daf 99 that even though pit and rim combine to ten, nevertheless above on top is not reshut ha-yachid and we do not say for others he makes a partition for himself — all the more so — see there; and to resolve all this it appears Acharonim hold certainly according to what the Gemara concludes Shabbos there where Ulla said if for others he makes a partition for himself — all the more so; and certainly even if the rim is not ten high we say thus if for others he makes a partition for himself — all the more so; and even on top is reshut ha-yachid; and what Tosafos challenged why mention twice pit and rim combine to ten — explain thus: since the examiner there in Shabbos first asks R' Yochanan on a wall in reshus harabbim ten high and concludes Ulla if for others he makes a partition for himself — all the more so; and then concludes R' Yochanan himself said thus; if so perforce R' Yochanan retracted, for initially he did not hold this reasoning if for others he makes a partition for himself — all the more so; and afterward concludes this reasoning; if so one may say what R' Yochanan answers in Eruvin deals with proximity and teaches pit and rim combine to ten — why mention twice; for why inform us in Shabbos twice — one may say as Tosefta Shabbat wrote it teaches on top is reshut ha-yachid; but according to what Ulla concludes and R' Yochanan retracted and holds this a fortiori if for others he makes a partition for himself — all the more so — then even on top is reshut ha-yachid; therefore R' Yochanan actually retracted also from his resolution in Eruvin, only also explaining like Rav Huna dealing with four away from the wall and the rim itself ten high — therefore we do not hear from there pit and rim combine to ten; therefore needed to inform us in Shabbos; but if so why not inform us in Shabbos regarding b'dieved if he took out liable and why not inform us the permission even l'chatchila to bring from it to reshut ha-yachid such as Eruvin's case of pit adjacent to wall and the like; automatically we know all the more liable; therefore proven l'chatchila permission pit and rim do not combine to ten to make reshut ha-yachid since we require encircled on all sides with rim — we are concerned he will err thinking even not encircled he will say if encircled on one or two sides with a tel he will say it is reshut ha-yachid; therefore they decreed even fully encircled on all sides also forbidden l'chatchila to take from it to reshut ha-yachid — only regarding Torah liability it is reshut ha-yachid; therefore Tur and Shulchan Aruch omitted this law pit and rim combine to permit l'chatchila; and through this there was room to resolve Tosefta Shabbat's challenge on Gittin chapter 2 on five-high mound and five-high partition for Rashi there — one may say there it goes only for us and therefore one view holds l'chatchila permission mound five and partition five do not combine; for b'dieved liability from Torah pit and rim combine and the other holds even l'chatchila permission they combine; and this Eruvin case is Rav Huna there; and from Shabbos no proof except from Torah it is reshut ha-yachid not d'rabbanan to permit l'chatchila; therefore they argue there; however Tur and Shulchan Aruch explain in Gittin explicitly Tosafos there and in pit and rim hold d'rabbanan it is not reshut ha-yachid; therefore they omitted this; and if so all the more for eruv partition law pit and small adjacent mound do not combine as above in my humble opinion; and I have no time to elaborate; perhaps God will grant me time later to explain more; examine well:`,
  },
  yad: {
    "1:_": `As Magen Avraham s.k. 3 wrote — and when coming in reshus harabbim air. It appears he means even in the first case when the rim is not ten high — then it comes to reshus harabbim air; even though there is prohibition as written seif 2 — nevertheless no liability; therefore they did not decree rim ten high lest not high because also when not high there is no liability since bound in his hand:`,
  },
};

export const SIM359 = {
  mech: {
    "1:main": `The law of a rechavah behind houses. And in it is one seif: A rechavah behind houses larger than beit se'ah that was not enclosed for dwelling — one may not move objects in it except within four amot; and if he opened an opening to it from his house and afterward enclosed it, even if there is a threshing floor between it and the house it is enclosure for dwelling: {Rama: And what we are not careful to move objects in courtyards behind houses — because nowadays they are by default enclosed for dwelling as explained above regarding karpef (private opinion)}`,
  },
  beer: {
    "1:א": `Eruvin 24 — statement of R' Kahana`,
    "1:ב": `There — statement of R' Nachman`,
  },
  biur: {
    "1:_": `Rechavah, etc. — know there are four names in this matter: karmelit, karpef, rechavah, chatzer. Karmelit d'oraisa is a valley without public traffic; karmelit d'rabbanan is karpef more than beit se'ah not enclosed for dwelling — for by law it is full reshut ha-yachid and rabbinically is like karmelit [nevertheless one moves from one to another within less than four amot as siman 346 seif 3; but from this karpef to chatzer forbidden as siman 372 seif 1]; and there karpef includes whether more than se'ah or beit se'ah enclosed for dwelling or not enclosed for dwelling. Chatzer before houses is certainly enclosed for dwelling and perforce even many korim is full reshut ha-yachid even d'rabbanan. Karpef that is only beit se'ah precisely and not enclosed for dwelling — even though called karpef — nevertheless permitted to move throughout and even to chatzer permitted; but to house forbidden; and likewise to karmelit or karpef more than beit se'ah also forbidden even of one person. Karpef more than beit se'ah enclosed for dwelling [even if holding many korim likewise] or less than beit se'ah and not enclosed for dwelling — even to house permitted to move, for it is considered like chatzer enclosed for dwelling; and all the more rechavah enclosed for dwelling certainly the law is thus. Rechavah that is beit se'ah precisely even though not enclosed for dwelling — nevertheless permitted to move even from it to house. All this is Semag's words in Mishbetzot Zahav:`,
  },
  mb: {
    "1:א": `(1) Rechavah behind houses — their custom was to leave empty space before houses and behind houses; that before houses is called chatzer and that behind houses is called rechavah; their custom was to encircle them with partitions; and behold the part called chatzer is certainly enclosed for dwelling since customary to do there all house uses; perforce even if more than beit se'ah and even ten korim permitted to move throughout and even from house into it [if one person or two who made eruv together] for one domain; but rechavah presumably not enclosed for dwelling since not customary to use there house uses so much; perforce its law is like karpef regarding more than beit se'ah [karpef is what they make far from the city — an enclosed place to store wood and the like]; and now we explain Shulchan Aruch's words rechavah behind, etc. — namely he enclosed this empty space with three partitions and attached them to his house wall:`,
    "1:ב": `(2) And was not enclosed for dwelling — that he did not open in the wall an opening to the rechavah before enclosing:`,
    "1:ג": `(3) Except within four amot — as law of other karpef not enclosed for dwelling as above siman 358 seif 1; and all the more forbidden to move from it to house; but if the enclosure is only se'ah it has no karpef law and permitted to move from it even to house since not a domain completely separate from the house like karpef even though not enclosed for dwelling:`,
    "1:ד": `(4) Even if there is a threshing floor, etc. — meaning even if there was a threshing floor behind his house before he enclosed with three partitions we do not say that because of the threshing floor an opening was opened in the house wall and there is no opening to the rechavah; rather by default opened to rechavah and behold it is enclosed for dwelling and permitted to move throughout and even from it to his house:`,
    "1:ה": `(5) In courtyards behind houses — meaning the rechavah above:`,
  },
  ma: {
    "1:_": `More than beit se'ah. But beit se'ah has no karpef law and permitted to move from it to house (Beit Yosef siman 358 Ritva):`,
  },
  mh: {
    "1:_": `(s.k. 1) More than, etc. — has no karpef law; for in karpef even though only beit se'ah it is permitted to move in the karpef itself but forbidden to move from it to house; here the rechavah law is lighter than karpef law:`,
  },
  er: {
    "1:_": `[1] More than, etc. But beit se'ah has no karpef law and permitted to move from it to house:`,
  },
  kaf: {
    "1:א": `A) [Seif 1] Rechavah behind houses, etc. Their custom was to leave empty space behind and before houses; that behind called rechavah and before called chatzer; and behold that before houses called chatzer is certainly enclosed for dwelling since customary to do there all house uses; perforce even if like beit kor or korim permitted to move throughout as written afterward in Mishbetzot Zahav and even from house into it if one person or two if they made eruv; but rechavah behind houses not customary to use for house needs so much and presumably not enclosed for dwelling; perforce if more than se'ah its law is like karpef as Shulchan Aruch wrote.`,
    "1:ב": `A) And know — four names in this matter karmelit karpef rechavah chatzer. Karmelit d'oraisa is valley without public traffic. Karmelit d'rabbanan — karpef more than se'ah not enclosed for dwelling — for from Torah full reshut ha-yachid and d'rabbanan is like karmelit. And enclosed for dwelling more than se'ah called karpef; and beit se'ah or less even not enclosed for dwelling called karpef. Rechavah behind houses also more than se'ah karmelit d'rabbanan without enclosure for dwelling. Chatzer before houses enclosed for dwelling even many korim reshut ha-yachid even d'rabbanan. And karmelit valley with karpef more than se'ah not enclosed — move from one to another less than four amot as siman 346 seif 3; but from this karpef to chatzer forbidden as siman 372 seif 1. Karpef beit se'ah without enclosure for dwelling — called karpef and move throughout and from it to karmelit forbidden and even to karpef more than se'ah forbidden. And from it to chatzer permitted; from it to house — no, even one person as siman 372 Magen Avraham 1; and it appears to me specifically se'ah called karpef — behold less than se'ah no karpef name upon it and permitted from it to house even without enclosure for dwelling. Behold enclosed for dwelling even many korim permitted from this karpef to house — for all enclosed for dwelling is like chatzer considered and one domain with house for one person. And know karpef is far from city and rechavah behind houses; and according to those who say karpef also behind houses forbidden — one may say karpef is made in form unlike rechavah with shorter fence and the like or made for wood and things used only at distant times unlike rechavah. Mishbetzot Zahav:`,
  },
};
